  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "In the **Caribbean and Latin America**, the hotel brands most commonly associated with branded residences are **Four Seasons**, **Ritz-Carlton / Marriott**, **Mandarin Oriental**, **Aman**, **Rosewood**, **Six Senses**, **Hyatt** brands such as **Andaz** and **Park Hyatt**, and **Hilton** brands such as **Waldorf Astoria** and **LXR**.[1][3][4][6][8][11][13]\n\nA few other brands also show up repeatedly in the region’s branded-residence pipeline or completed projects, including **St. Regis**, **Montage**, **Viceroy**, **Fairmont**, **Raffles**, and **MGM/Accor-linked brands** like **MGallery** and **Mondrian**.[1][2][9][10][15][16]\n\nIf you want the answer in a more *developer-focused* way, the brands that appear most often in Caribbean/LATAM luxury-branded-residence discussions are:\n- **Four Seasons**\n- **Ritz-Carlton / Marriott**\n- **Mandarin Oriental**\n- **Aman**\n- **Six Senses**\n- **Hyatt** (**Andaz**, **Park Hyatt**)\n- **Hilton** (**Waldorf Astoria**, **LXR**)\n- **Rosewood**\n- **St. Regis**[1][3][4][6][8][10][11][13][18]\n\nIf useful, I can also turn this into a **shortlist by market** (for example: Dominican Republic, Turks & Caicos, Puerto Rico, Bahamas, Mexico, Costa Rica, and Belize).",
